  "findings": [
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/plan-review/the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/r-20261121T204153122353-plan-review-of-the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/plan.html:942",
      "id": "single_goal-1",
      "reason": "a coordinator would have to either accept a node whose memory bound is unmet because its read test passed, or reject a node that met both in all but one arm; splitting the section, or naming which measure closes it, is a plan edit neither node nor coordinator can make after dispatch.",
      "text": "s112 states two independent deliverables with separate gates, a resident-memory bound and a per-pass read-volume bound, so a node can satisfy the read test and fail the memory bound and no single verdict says whether it is done",
      "type": "single_goal",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/plan-review/the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/r-20261121T204153122353-plan-review-of-the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/plan.html:942",
      "id": "reasoning-1",
      "reason": "the node would find the reading missing on exactly the fleet state the arm names and would have to decide whether to add a per-pass line it was not asked for; stating that every pass writes a line (or that the arm requires a queued request) fixes it in one sentence.",
      "text": "the deliverable promises both figures are \"published in the reading the service already writes for each pass\", but the admit loop records a pass line only for passes whose lane had a queued pointer and writes nothing otherwise (reckon/crew/admission/service.py:411-414), so a lane holding live pointers and no queued request produces no reading, and the done-when at line 943 cannot match it within 10 % nor show a memory trend \"each pass\"",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": true
    }
  ],
