  "rubric_items": {
    "anchors_resolve": "pass \u2014 36c098539b resolves and is an ancestor of main; the two run ids s110 and s111 cite (r-20261121T122055396740-review-of-wito-yoke-fd5d2783f078 and r-20261121T152554772571-review-of-icm-iron-field-source-cfb786340d69-figure) both resolve under ~/.config/reckon/crew/archive/runs, and the record s111 says was filed is present in the reviewed run's review-records directory naming that review run.",
    "done_when": "pass \u2014 each of the four nodes names a measure and a negative control pinned to \"main after 36c098539b\", which resolves on main; s109's and s110's controls now fix the revision the earlier review found unpinned, and every arm's log, revision and closing EXIT= line are stated.",
    "evidence_paths": "pass \u2014 every arm's log sits under the run directory with its revision, literal command and closing EXIT= line, and s112 requires the before/after figures in the plan's landed record rather than in a scratch path.",
    "naming": "pass \u2014 the four test filenames describe the behaviour they measure, and no plan labels, stage names, ticket numbers or changelog prose reached the sections' text or symbols.",
    "reasoning": "a finding \u2014 s112's deliverable rests on a per-pass reading the admit service writes only when its lane had a queued pointer, so the figure the live arm must match is absent on the fleet state the arm names.",
    "single_goal": "a finding \u2014 s112 carries a resident-memory bound and a per-pass read-volume bound as two separately gated deliverables in one section.",
    "wiring": "pass \u2014 s109-s112 declare no depends-on and each is independently buildable; the upstream work they rest on (the subscriber of s8, the pointer memos of s96/s102/s103, the run-store memo of s108) is declared done, so no missing edge would hold or mis-order them."
  },
